"""Opening brackets, strongest in prose/math and weaker in function calls.

Predict zero away from bracket tokens. For an opener, use its spacing and
attached text, plus the previous token's category. Each context tuple gives
scores for spaced ' (', bare '(', and '(' joined to a variable. No vocabulary
IDs or word-specific activation table are used; document boundaries reset state.
